<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Futong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1363</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Futong was a leader of the Red Turban rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-shantong">Han Shantong</a> was killed in 1351, he continued the revolt, and in 1355 he enthroned Han's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-liner">Han Lin'er</a> as emperor of a restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> at Bozhou. He held real power in the regime until he was killed in 1363 during an attack by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-shicheng">Zhang Shicheng</a>'s forces.</p></div>
